WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.500
Want to rest somewhere for a bit?

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.190
Yeah, good idea.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.400
Want a parfait?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.390
Yeah!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:13.950
Look out!

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.620
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.620
So the Ueno incident

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.120
involved the same Willwear as the 
ones in Akasaka and Ochanomizu?

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:25.970
Yes.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.840
The footprints and damage 
caused by strikes are the same.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.370
A few minutes before,

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.590
security cameras near the scene 
recorded this footage.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.340
It disappeared?

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.050
Optical camouflage?

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.880
Huh? Is that available for civilian use?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.640
The base is an Aoki 
Electrical Industries XP5540.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.150
It's available as an option.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.860
Forensics analyzed footprints believed 
to belong to the Willwear

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.610
and found microscopic organisms.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.580
These organisms are only found 
in a few locations in the city.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.040
Where?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.250
Here, in the quicksand zone.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.360
That's... the Yamanote Immigrant District?

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.080
Which means the criminal is...

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.960
Would an illegal immigrant 
really own a Willwear?

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.930
So the suspect either deals with industrial 
waste or is taking advantage of the chaos?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.690
On that note, we have a spy job for you!

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.350
Huh? For me?

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.740
Sorry, but given the location, 
we couldn't get permission...

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.990
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.500
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.690
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.830
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.110
<b>File 8: The Stranger in the Wind</b>

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.730
Are you sure

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.980
you should be following me, 
when Unit 8 hasn't received permission?

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.220
I have the afternoon off.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.940
If I follow you in my free time, 
that's no one's business.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:13.500
But...

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.800
Funasaka-san wants us to take turns 
backing you up every day.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.260
I see.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.740
Whoops...

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.790
There's still this much trash?

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.530
It's partly politics.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.210
But many immigrants, both 
legal and illegal, moved in

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.920
before the government 
had decided on a policy.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.680
It's a gray zone now, out of everyone's reach.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.210
What's that?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.540
They're made of empty cans.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.180
That's a lot of work, for a place like this.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.010
Are you the one who cleaned up this area?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.850
I wasn't going to steal it...

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.480
I see.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.530
You don't understand me.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.670
I speak the language.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.740
Just don't butt in.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.950
Um, we had some questions...

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.320
They have their own lives down here, huh?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.540
You don't work for the city government of Tokyo.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.060
Who said you could take this trash?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.020
What are your demands?

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.520
Our conditions are simple.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.480
Hand over anything you find that's worth money.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.200
And from now on, if you take
anything, go through us.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.110
Hey! You're going to properly dispose of it, right?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.590
Who the hell are you?!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.460
Stop it.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.500
Weren't you on the Nippori team?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.650
That's enough.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.630
Tell me the name of your office.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.620
Where is it?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.290
What? They don't work for a gang?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.800
And they're pretty nasty, too.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.720
It was a long time ago.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.310
Really? You made contact with the locals?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.820
Yes, someone was indeed selling 
rubble through illegal channels.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.600
They may be linked to the 
Kanto Shared Ownership Association.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:43.320
Tomorrow, I'll talk to the people 
living here illegally.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.780
But I didn't find any clues about the Willwear.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.420
Well, there's no need to hurry on that.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.410
As for your support tomorrow...

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.690
Huh? I'll be alone tomorrow?

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:54.880
Okay, understood.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.050
Hey, boy...

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.760
You got the hookup?

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.530
Um, this side of the wall is Tokyo City.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.010
Do you have a passport or an ID?

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.080
What are you talking about?

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.260
You're the guy, right? Hook me up!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.110
Huh?

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.980
The thing from before!

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.470
What "thing"?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.730
Wait! Let me talk to—

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.900
Ow...

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.040
Mister...

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.940
You can have these. Talk to me.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.450
Those are mine!

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.950
I hate to be pushy, but you do have 
transport permits for these, right?

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.540
And be sure to dispose of—

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.500
Man, you're so cautious.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.370
Well, we'll take care of the rest.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.770
That's their truck.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:45.590
Can you see it?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:48.050
Yes, Haruka-kun will track it.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.260
If they're dumping illegally, 
we'll arrest them later.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.700
Thank you.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.660
You bastard!

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.900
How many times do I have to say it?

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.350
To sell things in someone else's country, 
you've gotta pay the locals!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:04.520
Stop it!

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.710
Who the hell are you?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.480
You're going too far.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.410
It's fine.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.080
These guys don't even have a country!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.630
Stop it!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.540
You're protecting an illegal immigrant?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.370
They don't want to be illegal.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.830
Hey, that's enough.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.630
Piss this guy off, and you'll have to 
deal with the gang that backs him.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.590
No, I...

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.040
Fine!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.420
You'd better pay up next time, Atin.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.190
Why did you save me?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.650
If something unfair is happening 
to someone, of course I'll help.

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.570
Where did you come from?

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:53.860
No, if you don't want to tell me—

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:54.780
Carupanuba.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.910
That's where I'm from. Do you know it?

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.000
No, not really.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.030
It's a small country to the south.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.870
The country is poor, but peaceful.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.130
Or it used to be.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:07.540
Used to be?

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:11.640
Until it was taken over by a dictator 
who liked the geopolitical advantage

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:15.890
and money from running a country 
directly under the equator.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.770
You ran?

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:18.890
Or I'd have died.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:21.770
I see.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.060
No, that's the wrong way.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.630
This is the way I do it.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.210
You're stubborn.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.670
So are you.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.840
I'm Sena. Sena Souichirou.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.600
Sorry to say this after you helped me,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.880
but I don't want you invading my privacy.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.860
Would you leave?

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.520
Carupanuba...

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:06.270
That name makes things complicated.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.520
Didn't that country make the Willwear 
involved in the Rudra incident?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.180
It's a dictatorship,

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.740
but the Japanese government takes 
pains to stay on its good side.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.160
They do?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.680
You didn't know, Sena-san?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.370
Sorry, the <i>Garbage Disposal Times</i> is all I read.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:33.460
<b>Geosynchronous Orbit

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:33.460
<b>Orbital Ring 

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.350
<i>That's the plan for the space elevator, right?</i>

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.560
<i>The Takao Tower?</i>

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.400
<i>That demonstration is intended 
for the whole world!</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.300
<i>And a rumor says it's been decided 
at a political level that,</i>

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.920
<i>once the demonstration ends, they'll build 
a more permanent one in Carupanuba.</i>

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.210
<i>Do you believe it? Or not?</i>

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.930
I think I understand.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:46.840
It's right below the equator, 
which makes building an elevator easy.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:50.050
Once it's done, huge sums 
of money will be involved,

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.610
so the ruling party does all 
it can to keep them happy.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.150
Even Governor Inagi can't do anything about it.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.860
So, Sena-kun,

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.320
this Atin from Carupanuba is involved?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.660
No, I'm not sure.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:03.790
But...

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:06.560
We found someone who looked like a witness.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.080
I was planning to look into it again later, but...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.530
But first—

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:11.790
Wait, Sena-kun.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:14.210
That Willwear has appeared in Gotanda.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.250
Shinagawa Ward, East Gotanda, Second Street.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.220
A vehicle was destroyed while 
in motion, causing injuries.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.140
No sign of any suspect.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.600
We believe it's the invisible Willwear.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:30.810
Displaying footage.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:32.770
Oh, dear...

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.100
He might have gotten away by now.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:40.440
Atin!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:42.910
Atin!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.120
Need something?

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.040
Atin...

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.750
Oh, um... I was just seeing if 
you wanted to have lunch...

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.650
I bought some donuts.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.430
They're in the parking lot there.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.030
I'll get them now.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.810
This is nice.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.020
It's so clean.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.230
That's enough to tell me I can trust you.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:20.780
I'm sorry...

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:21.660
I'll get that.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:25.670
Your family?

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.080
Forget that, sing!

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:31.430
Japanese sing at times like this, right?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.200
Or dance naked?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.170
You're a weird drunk.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.410
Drunk?

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.450
This is a drink?

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:40.180
You've never had alcohol?

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.680
It was forbidden in my country.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.850
What was your country like?

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:48.250
Constant civil wars.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.790
People dying all the time.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.300
Is that funny?

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:54.840
No, it's not. I didn't know.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:55.940
Of course not.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.890
In some countries, it's a big deal when 
a few people die from terrorism,

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.860
and in some countries, no one cares,

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.620
no matter how many die.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.510
Still, I wanted to make it better.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:12.510
I tried to support our talentless politicians.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:14.070
Support them?

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.170
That was your job?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.520
I don't know.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:23.000
In the end, the dictator tried to rely 
on Japan to rebuild the economy.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.700
I wonder what the right answer was...

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.850
Why did you save me?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.640
I told you.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.020
I couldn't just let something unfair happen—

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.050
You're lying.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.840
Something unfair is happening to everyone.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.780
At least, in my country.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.530
That's why we all pretend we don't see it.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.930
That's different.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:45.820
Yes.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.030
People have ideals.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.420
That's why...

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.100
That's why...

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:52.990
I...

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.510
You've lived an earnest life, haven't you?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.850
I haven't had strong beliefs 
to anchor me like you.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.050
I've just gone with the flow,

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.930
living life as it came.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.060
I have dreams.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.050
About when my little brother and sister died.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.510
I couldn't do anything.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.920
When I was chased out of my own country,

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:29.080
I took my young brother and sister with me.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.040
I used all my money to buy a little boat.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.330
We saw the morning sun 
many times on the open sea.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:36.820
It was beautiful.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.790
But I started to get scared,

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:43.500
and we started to run out 
of things to eat and drink.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.150
Even when the cans were empty,

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.960
they'd put them upside-down 
on top of their cups,

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.820
hoping some tiny drop of 
liquid would come out.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.320
When they were totally empty, 
I made pinwheels out of them.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.650
They loved that.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.860
It didn't make anything better.

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.160
But it really made them happy.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.160
It made them smile.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.690
One day, a big ship passed.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:17.940
My brother and sister were too 
exhausted to even speak,

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.300
but I yelled as loud as I could.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:21.700
But...

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.550
They didn't notice?

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:27.180
They were so close, they had to.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.300
Who wants to deal with a boat of refugees?

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:34.970
Rain...

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.480
If only it had rained...

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.880
Have you ever hated anyone?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.030
Well, a few times.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.360
Have you wanted to kill them?

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:48.500
No way.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.360
I have.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:53.130
Sometimes, I think I'm about to lose control.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.380
If I only had the chance...

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:57.830
You want revenge? On whom?

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:00.790
I'm joking.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.750
Atin,

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.910
why not make a place for yourself?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:07.910
With different scenery—

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.340
There is nowhere for me.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:11.010
Someday,

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.520
they'll kick me out of this place, too.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.180
Yo.

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:21.950
Your shift is already over.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:23.990
I'm taking a day off!

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:29.150
I ate yours before, so I got you these.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.400
<b>Super-Spicy Donuts 
Yum</b>

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:35.450
If you think that's what "etiquette" 
means, you're wrong.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:44.960
It's his way of remembering 
his brother and sister.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.600
The boss says to return to Kichijouji

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.850
if nothing suspicious happens by noon.

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:50.650
All right.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.340
What's your take on him?

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.550
Innocent... is what I'd like to believe.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:55.950
No motive.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.060
I'm not so sure.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:00.050
He has nothing left to lose, right?

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.640
He's lost his home and family.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.810
He wants to vent his anger, 
but no one's available.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.190
It would only take something to give him—

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.190
Don't talk like you understand!

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:14.060
I lost my hometown, too.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.740
You shouldn't get weirdly attached.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:20.240
You won't notice if he's lying to you.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.520
I'm the one who's lying to him.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.060
Oh... You're leaving?

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:33.220
Yeah. I've finished my investigation 
of the resources here.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.200
Would you take this?

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.180
If you don't mind.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:39.140
No, but...

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.310
It made me happy

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.600
that you saved me.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.240
You are

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.360
the first person to look me in 
the eye since I came here.

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:55.190
Atin, I talked about this before...

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:57.740
Never mind...

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:00.330
Bye.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.630
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.090
<b>Illegal Immigrants Forced Into Dangerous Work</b>

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.090
These are the illegal businessmen 
you were tracking, aren't they?

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:15.050
Yeah, I'm glad we finished that up, but...

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.010
We're not seeing that 
invisible attacker anymore.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.150
That's right...

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.220
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.220
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:22.430
There.

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:26.470
This certifies that you're contracted with us.

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:27.650
Thank you.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.170
What's next? Application for refugee status?

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.860
Or a change in residency rights?

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:38.460
Well, first I have to find out 
how he got into the country.

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:42.050
If he's going to work at the company, 
I'll need the director's permission.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.760
Boss! The invisible Willwear!

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:49.670
People have been injured!

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.550
Fortunately, none of their injuries 
were life-threatening.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.690
Lucky us!

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:57.510
Lucky us? Haruka-chan, there were casualties.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.620
That's not what I meant.

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:02.730
There are rainclouds near the scene.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.790
Oscar I, after launching from 
the mobile command vehicle,

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:08.690
keep firing toward the sky.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:09.900
Roger.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.980
Matching radius and position data.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.190
Data matched.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:16.400
Shoot!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.590
Now, Oscar II.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:23.410
Launch!

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:24.240
Launching.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.920
Yes! We've created an artificial storm!

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:42.810
Oscar II, head straight for Kitashinagawa Bridge!

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.430
The PCs are trapping him!

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:45.680
On it!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.320
He's on the bridge?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:54.860
Yeah.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:56.630
This is it.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.320
It's surrounded by the quicksand zone.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:01.160
His Willwear will sink.

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.830
Where is he?

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.010
He stopped. He must have caught on.

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:07.830
He realized that we were watching his 
feet splashing through puddles.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.230
If we know he's on the bridge...

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.010
Wait. Don't move at random.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:13.130
Kyoukai-san,

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:17.370
how long will the battery last in rain mode?

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:24.470
It depends on how much he has it 
charged, so I can't say for certain,

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:27.020
but a new battery, at full charge, 
can last six hours.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.320
You're going to wait?

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.920
The rain's letting up!

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.310
There he goes!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.030
What? You missed?!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:40.820
I grazed him.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.350
That should have damaged him!

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:43.620
I'll go on ahead!

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:56.980
Where are you?

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:58.050
Where are you?

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:13.480
Atin?

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.400
Atin, is that you?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:22.860
Atin!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.970
There he is!

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:33.300
He's in plain sight!

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:35.070
Is his battery dead?

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:36.090
Oscar I?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.090
I thought it would be you, Sena.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.770
I just had a feeling, for some reason.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.820
So I tested you.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:51.100
If you noticed the cans, I'd know it was you.

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:54.350
I thought this might be fate.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:02.030
Why did the Japanese government 
join hands with that dictator?!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.700
If they hadn't...

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:08.660
Atin, that doesn't excuse what you did.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.700
Look at all this rain...

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:15.310
So much rain.

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:17.790
Back then...

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:22.380
If it had rained like this...

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.850
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:30.850
Deportation to his home country?!

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:33.310
Is this another of those extralegal measures?!

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:35.910
It appears they prioritize good 
relations with Carupanuba,

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.740
and have agreed to the request.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:41.280
Evidently, he was a leader of 
the anti-government forces.

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:42.870
Either way,

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:45.740
he won't survive once he gets back.

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:51.510
I wanted to get a clue about who 
gave him that Willwear, at least.

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:54.280
Well, maybe we got lucky that

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.950
we caught him there at all.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:57.500
That's right...

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:01.640
We were lucky the battery ran out there!

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.090
Huh? I didn't tell you?

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:08.430
His Willwear battery still had plenty of charge.

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:10.890
Then why...

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:15.850
<i>Atin, if that was your way of 
repaying me for saving you...</i>

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:23.510
<i>It's hard to live an earnest life, isn't it?</i>

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.870
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:55.170 --> 00:23:56.730
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:55.870 --> 00:24:09.000
File 9: Unit 8, Don't Mobilize

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:58.330
At last, I got to say it!

00:23:58.330 --> 00:24:01.000
Does that mean you have a 
big role next time, Emilia?

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.740
But doesn't being in the preview like this

00:24:02.740 --> 00:24:04.630
mean something crazy will happen to you?

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:05.630
<i>Kuwabara, kuwabara...</i>

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:06.750
What's that?

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:08.870
It's an ancient Japanese spell.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:08.860
<b>Kyuu Kyuu Nyo Ritsu Ryou</b>
